#3800
The Sluicekeeper's Niche~
A low side chamber has been cut into the dry stone beside the sluice
shaft. A waist-high ledge serves as a worktable, while empty iron pegs
and shallow tool scars mark the wall above it. Old tally cuts record
water levels and gate inspections in a hand long since forgotten. Damp
air enters from the east, carrying the steady rush of the lower drains.
~
