#3801
The Lower Sluice Shaft~
The iron ladder from the upper underworks ends on a narrow stone shelf
above a circular sluice chamber. Water pours down the walls and
vanishes through a heavy grate set into the floor. The fitted masonry
is older than the brickwork above and blackened by centuries of mineral
stain. Deep claw marks score the grate, and a broad nest of rope, rags,
and broken tools has been dragged into one corner.
~
