#3802
The Drowned Collector~
Below the grate, several streams converge inside a broad stone
collector. Cold runoff reaches nearly to the knee before spilling
north through an ancient arched conduit. The walls are massive dressed
blocks rather than brick, their joints packed with black mineral crust.
Old bronze direction marks point toward districts whose names have
vanished from common use.
~
