#3803
The Ruptured Stone Conduit~
The collector narrows into an immense arched conduit bound at intervals
with old iron hoops. Smaller feeder channels have broken through the
walls at uneven heights, spilling thin curtains of cold water into the
main flow. Scratches, gnawed bones, and greasy nesting fiber gather on
the higher ledges. Northward, a collapsed section opens into a chamber
far larger than the surrounding waterworks.
~
