#3804
The Great Confluence~
Several ages of Midgaard's buried construction meet here. The southern
stone conduit empties into a broad chamber while a deeper channel
continues north beneath carved funerary arches. High overhead, a patch
of false masonry hides a narrow opening that does not belong to the
waterworks. The current has worn the floor smooth around fragments of
carved burial stone washed in from somewhere ahead.
~
