#3805
The Burrow Behind the Masonry~
A hidden break above the confluence leads into a cramped passage chipped
through old foundation stone by patient hands and crude tools. The
tunnel twists upward between buried walls, reinforced with stolen boards
and pieces of iron scavenged from the drains. Candle soot stains shallow
niches along the route. Whoever made this passage knew exactly where the
city watch and sluicekeepers were least likely to look.
~
