#3807
The Ossuary Spillway~
Beyond the confluence, the drains enter a much older vaulted spillway.
Dry ledges flank a dark central channel where fragments of bone turn
slowly in the current. Recesses in the walls resemble burial niches
more than work alcoves, though several were broken open when later
masons cut the watercourse through this place. The eastern arch leads
deeper into architecture that predates the city's newer drains.
~
