#3808
The Processional Drain~
The passage east was once something other than a drain. Narrow gutters
were cut later through a stone floor worn smooth by countless footsteps,
and shallow funerary niches line both walls behind the newer stonework.
Broken reliefs show robed figures carrying lamps toward a doorway farther
east. Water whispers through the added channels while the old procession
seems to continue in stone.
~
