#3809
The Sealed Catacomb Threshold~
The drainage passage ends before a monumental stone threshold buried
beneath later construction. Its eastern doorway has been sealed with
fitted blocks, iron cramps, and pale mortar unlike anything used in the
surrounding drains. Weathered burial script circles the frame, while
newer marks warn workmen not to breach it. Cold air seeps through
hairline cracks in the seal. Whatever lies beyond belongs to an older
Midgaard that someone took great care to leave buried.
~
