#3899
The Silent Survey Vault~
Beyond the hidden panel lies a dry stone chamber untouched by the rushing
water outside. A narrow table is carved directly from one wall, and
faded measuring marks cover the surrounding blocks. Brittle scraps of
parchment cling beneath a stone weight, showing fragments of foundation
lines and forgotten drains beneath Midgaard. Slaive's later charcoal
notations cross several of the older measurements, revealing that he
found and used this forgotten survey vault as part of his refuge.
~
